# Wireframe: Cycle List

## Purpose & Flow Context

The Cycle List displays all cycles (sprints/iterations) for the current team, updating in real-time as other team members create, activate, update, or complete cycles via WebSocket events. Entry: user navigates to Cycles section. Exit: user clicks a cycle card to view detail, or navigates away. This wireframe covers the list-level layout and how real-time cycle events (activation, completion) manifest on this screen.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Cycle List sits in the main content area.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Shared app-shell header | See header-connection-status.wireframes |
| Toolbar | Search, status filter, "New Cycle" button | Below header |
| Active Cycle Banner | Highlights the currently active cycle | Prominent, full width |
| Cycle List | Vertical list of cycle cards | Scrollable, below banner |
| Empty State | When no cycles | Full width in content area |

